    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Conyza varia</b></i> is a species of flowering plants of the family Asteraceae. The species is endemic to Cape Verde. It is listed as an endangered plant by the IUCN. First described as <i>Erigeron varius</i> by Philip Barker Webb, it was placed in the genus <i>Conyza</i> by Hiram Wild in 1969. Its local name is <i>marcelinha</i> or <i>tabua</i>, <i>tabuinha</i>. The plant plays a role in traditional medicine: crushed and heated leaves are used to treat external inflammations.",
